<title>UK: NIGERIA CUTS SEPT BQ, RAISES FORCADOS PRICE.</title>
<headline>NIGERIA CUTS SEPT BQ, RAISES FORCADOS PRICE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigerian National Petroleum Corp announced crude</p>
<p>contract prices for September, trade sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>Following are new prices versus benchmark dated Brent.</p>
<p>		    Sept	  August     change</p>
<p>Bonny Light    +30 cts     +35 cts   dn  5 cts</p>
<p>Qua Iboe	 +30 cts     +35 cts   dn  5 cts</p>
<p>Forcados	 +20 cts     +15 cts   up  5 cts</p>
<p>Escravos	 +25 cts     +33 cts   dn  8 cts</p>
<p>Brass River    +35 cts     +38 cts   dn  3 cts</p>
<p>Pennington     +65 cts     +65 cts   unchanged</p>
<p>Bonny Medium   +8 cts	+5 cts    up  3 cts</p>
<p>NNPC left unchanged at five cents the cost of its option to price crude one week ahead of bill of lading.</p>
<p>An option for deferred pricing 14 days after bill of lading was also maintainted at five cents.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
